note SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
note Independent finite oracle: a two-outcome drafter accepts everything with p,
note or rejects the first token with 1-p, so E = 1 + k*p without a survival loop.
global lens ulong 7
global oparams ulong 4
fn oracle to ulong
best = ulong 0
be = ulong 1000000
bt = ulong 101
for r ulong 7
k = get lens r
if le add k 1 get oparams 2
if le add 100 mul r 10 get oparams 3
expect = add 1000000 mul k get oparams 0
cost = add 101 mul get oparams 1 mul k k
if gt mul expect bt mul be cost
best = k
be = expect
bt = cost
end
end
end
end
ret best
end
fn trialcase remain ulong to void
put oparams 2 remain
check eq sbegin 0 0
put scontrol 0 0
put scontrol 1 0
check eq sselect 1000 remain get oparams 3 7 2 0 0
check eq get decision 0 oracle
check le get decision 1 remain
check le get decision 2 32000000
scancel
end
fn sweep to void
fixture
put lens 0 0
put lens 1 1
put lens 2 2
put lens 3 4
put lens 4 8
put lens 5 16
put lens 6 31
for p ulong 5
put oparams 0 mul p 250000
for i ulong 31
put sprior i get oparams 0
end
for curve ulong 8
put oparams 1 curve
for r ulong 7
put srows add mul r 11 4 add 100 mul curve mul get lens r get lens r
end
for m ulong 2
put oparams 3 add 130 mul m 30
for i ulong 32
trialcase add i 1
end
end
end
end
end
fn main to int
sweep
ret finish
end
